<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6436" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cănālĭcŭlus</span></b> ,
		i, m. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cănālĭcŭla</span></b> ,
			ae, f. (ante- and post-class.), <i><span class="en">Varr. R.
			R. 3, 5, 14</span></i>; Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 198,
		7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 11, 2</span></i>; cf. canalis), dim.
		canalis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small channel</i>, <i>pipe</i>, or
				<i>gutter.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A water-channel</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10, 14
					<i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 8, 15,
				6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A channel of a triglyph</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The channel</i> or <i>groove of a
				catapult</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10,
			15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			In surgery, <i>a splint for broken bones</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 8, 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
